{
 "esm": "2.0.0",
 "metadata": {
 "name": "cam_rrtmg_lw",
 "description": "The CAM RRTMG longwave column solver (stage 2 of the EqESM project) as math, transcribed from the instrumented cam6_4_212 fork (components/cam/src/physics/rrtmg/aer_src/rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90, with the Pade tables of rrtmg_lw_init.f90:96-112, rrlw_tbl.f90 and the spectral data of rrtmg_lw_init.f90:187-189, 275, 308-323): the variable diffusivity angle secdiff(ibnd) = 1.66 for bands 1, 4 and 10-16 and the clamped a0 + a1*exp(a2*pwvcm) form for bands 2-3 and 5-9 (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:224-232), the McICA cloud scaling odcld = secdiff*taucmc, abscld = 1 - exp(-odcld), efclfrac = abscld*cldfmc and the icldlyr layer-cloud flag (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:255-271), the Pade-table gas and total layer transmittance laws (the tau_tbl/exp_tbl/tfn_tbl lookup tables of rrtmg_lw_init.f90:96-112 at the index itr = int(10000*odepth/(bpade + odepth) + 0.5), bpade = 1/0.278, with the quadratic expansion odepth - 0.5*odepth^2 branch below odepth = 0.06; the total optical depth odtot = odepth + odcld reuses the gas-law effective depth, which is the table tau_tbl(itr) on the gas table branch), the linear-in-tau Planck source laws bbd/bbugas/bbdtot/bbutot = plfrac*(blay + tfac*dplank) and the direction-matched layer sources gassrc = atrans*bbd and gassrc_up = atrans*bbugas (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:290-365, 416-418), the unified cloudy/clear down and up sweeps: the single recurrence rad' = rad - rad*A + gassrc + cldfmc*(bbdtot*atot - gassrc) with A = atrans + efclfrac*(1 - atrans) binding the down source gassrc on the down sweep and the up source gassrc_up on the up sweep (the Fortran up loop reassigns gassrc = bbugas*atrans at rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:416-418), which reduces to the clear-layer form rad + (bb - rad)*atrans with bb = bbd down and bb = bbugas up where the cloud quantities vanish (cldfmc = 0), and the clear-layer Planck factors bbd/bbugas (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:367-384, 416-427), the specular surface radiance rad0 + reflect*radld with rad0 = fracs(1,ig)*plankbnd(ib) of the bottom layer and reflect = 1 - semiss (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:403-407), the clear-sky streams: equal to the total streams at every interface while no cloud lies in the down path (iclddn = 0), computed separately below the first cloud (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:388-394, 432-438), the per-g-point flux scaling wtdiff*delwave(ib)*fluxfac of the band output (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:449-466; wtdiff = 0.5, fluxfac = pi*2e4, delwave of rrtmg_lw_init.f90:187-189) and the band-summed interface totals, and the heating rates heatfac*(fnet(l) - fnet(lev))/(pz(l) - pz(lev)) (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:480-499, heatfac = g*cday*1e-5/(cpair*1e-3) of rrtmg_lw_init.f90:211-212) converted to the CAM qrl = htr*cpair/86400 W/kg heating rates of radlw.F90:244-245. The models are composed by data: each model declares its inputs (parameters with dump-derived defaults); stage-3 composition will couple them by reference. All layer and interface axes are top-down: k = 1..33 (k = 1 the clear extra top layer above the model top), k_ifc = 1..34 (k_ifc = 1 TOA), the bottom-up kb = 1..34 (kb = 1 at the surface, reading the top-down layer 35 - kb for the up sweep), and the esd lev axis (1 = CAM top) carries the heating rates with the extra top layer dropped. The pins are the gated cam_rad_rtrnmc*.csv dump of the solver internals (the cam_dump_rtrnmc_* buffer of cam_dump_mod.F90, flushed at the radiation boundary): the expected values are dump columns only - taut/fracs/cldfmc/taucmc (cam_rad_rtrnmc.csv, one row per g-point and layer), planklay/planklev (cam_rad_rtrnmc_plank.csv/cam_rad_rtrnmc_planklev.csv, per band and layer/interface), plankbnd/semiss (cam_rad_rtrnmc_bnd.csv), pwvcm and pz (cam_rad_rtrnmc_scal.csv), the per-g-point flux contributions uflux/dflux/uclfl/dclfl (cam_rad_rtrnmc_ifc.csv), the totals totuflux/totdflux/totuclfl/totdclfl (the band-summed interface fluxes, the cam_rad_out_ifc.csv ful/fdl/fnl/fcnl columns are these mapped to the CAM interfaces) and the qrl/qrlc/flnsc/flntc heating rates (cam_rad_out.csv, cam_rad_scal.csv). The step-3 column is cloud-free (cldfmc = taucmc = 0 for every layer and g-point), so there icldlyr = iclddn = 0, the clear streams equal the total streams and uclfl = uflux, dclfl = dflux exactly; the step-41/45/47 McICA subcolumns carry clouds (every g-point has a cloud at layer k = 16 and some g-points further layers k = 17..30, cldfmc = 1, taucmc = 6e-3..2.9), so those tests exercise the cloudy branch - odcld/abscld/efclfrac, the icldlyr/iclddn flags and the unified update's cldfmc term - and the clear streams, equal to the total streams above the first cloud and computed separately below it (rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:388-394, 432-438). The four tests are the 1997-06-19 00/06/12/18 UTC radiation calls (dump steps 3, 41, 45, 47, the 3585/7185/10785/14385 s-of-day rows). Every expected value is selected (not derived) by extract_cam_rrtmg_lw_pins.py, and every test description cites the dump column and the RRTMG line.",
 "tags": [
  "atmosphere",
  "cam",
  "rrtmg",
  "longwave",
  "dump-pinned",
  "cesm"
 ],
