    {
     "id": "fluxes_step3",
     "description": "The rtrnmc heating-rate stage at step 3 (the 1997-06-19 00 UTC radiation call, tod 3585 s; defaults are the step-3 totals, no overrides). The fnet/fnetc laws, the htr_td/htrc_td layer heating rates (heatfac*(fnet(k_ifc+1) - fnet(k_ifc))/(pz(k_ifc+1) - pz(k_ifc)), rrtmg_lw_rtrnmc.f90:493-494, htr_td(34) = htrc_td(34) = 0), the CAM heating rates qrl/qrlc = htr_td(lev+1)*cpair*dps and the clear-sky surface/top net fluxes flnsc = fnetc(34), flntc = fnetc(2). Expected values are the cam_rad_out.csv qrl/qrlc columns and the cam_rad_scal.csv flnsc/flntc scalars (selected by extract_cam_rrtmg_lw_pins.py) at rel 1e-10 for the heating rates (measured max 2.8e-11: the fnet difference in the htr law cancels to ~1e-13 absolute, amplifying the ~1e-15 total residuals on the smallest rates) and rel 1e-12 for the nets (measured max 4.3e-15). The all-clear column (cldfmc = 0, see sweep_step3) makes qrl = qrlc, flnsc = flntc - fnetc(2) exactly.",
